               bringin' it down with another /X bit for you!

           this time it is called (for want of a better name..)

                          ! sUPER-fREE-LEECH !


What?

Simple... (as are most of my ideas). All it does is make files
freely downloadable if they fit the criteria.. ie if they are either
a special group release (eg QTX-#?) or if it has been uploaded into a
conference that you can designate as a "FREE DOWNLOAD" conference.
Supports up to 100 free-leech conferences and 100 group prefixes. (Should
be enough, right?)

Why?

I wanted one and couldnt find one. Sorry if I've stepped in on your turf
if you have made one already!

Where?

My underground dungeon that I call `home'. No place like it (probably just
as well!)

When?

Started on the 25th of August 1994. It's now the 25th of August 1994 (still).
Alright, so I've been adding bits in since then, but the bulk of the code is
still the stuff that took a couple of hours!

How?

Install the files that you have unpacked from the archive into their proper
directories. It should be easy enough to work that out. If you've installed
a few /X utils before, then you should have no problem doing the same with
this one!

Personal Configuration?

Yes! There's a few (very easy) things you will have to do to in order
to get it working properly on your set-up.
So load up CED (why use anything else?) and load in the file "FREE.CFG"
that came with the archive - you should've put it in DOORS:SUPERTOUCH/

Alright..lets get to work! In the example FREE.CFG file, the first 3 lines
are taken up by file prefixes. Any file that has this prefix will be made
a free-download for anyone else. You may have up to 100 different file
prefixes in your config file. This option is obviously (?) for boards that
want their group releases as free-downloads.

The line after your last file prefix must have the first 4 characters as
****
else this utility wont work properly.

The next line(s) are the names of the conferences that allow free-downloads
(These names are the ones used in the BBS:ConfConfig.info icon)

You may have up to 100 different conference names here.. (yes, pointless
having that many, I know! But who cares?)

The line after your last canference same must have the first 4 characters as
****
else this utility wont work properly. (Deja Vu?)


The following 5 lines are to do with text configuration.
You can change the language or whatever, its up to you! Neato!
All text must be between |'s, this is so you can have trailing & preceeding
spaces in the text lines.


  1) Text that is displayed to show what conference the user is in.

  2) Text that is displayed when the file does not fit the criteria
     of being made a free-leech file.

  3) Text that is displayed when the file is released by a certain
& 4) group (with a certain filename prefix.. eg QTX-   )
     The included example would output..

     < qUARTEX rELEASE! - mAKING xxxxxxxxx a fREE-LEECH! >

     where xxxxxxxxx is the name of the uploaded file.

  5) Text that is displayed when the file is uploaded into a free-leech
     conference (all uploads into it are made free-downloads)



Okay...that's it.. if all is going well, then when someone uploads a file,
it will go into sUPER-fREE-LEECH, and do its stuff.
s.F.L has only been tested on /X 4.3, so I cant guarentee it'll work on
anything else...
I dont expect you'll have any problems with this since it is all very basic.
If however you do experience that it isnt working properly, and you think
you've followed the instructions properly, then track me down and get me to
check it out.

NOTE2: If you use a filechecker/stripper such as MasterStripper from
       Delusion that adds a comment to the checked file, after
       sUPER-fREE-LEECH has run through and added one, it will
       not work. IE.. it WONT give the user free-downloads.
       All I can suggest is you change strippers (you know the sort I mean) :)
       A pity since MasterStripper is nice.

NOTE2: sUPER-fREE-LEECH will not add a comment into DIRx.. like some other
       utils. I cannot see any way to do this...yet. :)

END BITS:

If anyone has any suggestions to improve this small, versatile, courageous,
yet kind-hearted little AREXX-MUTHA-FUCKA, then get in touch with me somehow!
I shouldnt be too hard to track down.. just ask your local QTX member!

Anyone want a GUI configurator for sUPER-fREE-LEECH? :)




